l_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"fAD7gaDJxegE"},"source":["# **Gini Impurity**Gini Impurity\n","Before start working with Decision Trees, let's briefly explain how they work. The goal of their learning algorithms is always to find the best split for each node of the tree. But measuring the \"goodness\" of a given split is a subjective question so, in practice, different metrics are used for evaluating splits. One commonly used metric is Information Gain. The sklearn library we're gonna use implements Gini Impurity, another common measure, so let’s explain it.\n","\n","Gini Impurity measures the disorder of a set of elements. It is calculated as the probability of mislabelling an element assuming that the element is randomly labelled according the the distribution of all the classes in the set. Decision Trees will try to find the split which decreases Gini Impurity the most across the two resulting nodes. For the titanic example it can be calculated as follows (code should be explicit enough):"]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{"id":"25OQY-T4xkjl"},"source":["# Define function to calculate Gini Impurity\n","def get_gini_impurity(survived_count, total_count):\n","    survival_prob = survived_count/total_count\n","    not_survival_prob = (1 - survival_prob)\n","    random_observation_survived_prob = survival_prob\n","    random_observation_not_survived_prob = (1 - random_observation_survived_prob)\n","    mislabelling_survided_prob = not_survival_prob * random_observation_survived_prob\n","    mislabelling_not_survided_prob = survival_prob * random_observation_not_survived_prob\n","    gini_impurity = mislabelling_survided_prob + mislabelling_not_survided_prob\n","    return gini_impurity"],"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"ll7-Z2LpxmzK","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1623566224604,"user_tz":-480,"elapsed":198,"user":{"displayName":"北科大-張嘉芸","photoUrl":"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/AOh14GhcM20C68MTH2x-G3yrqTq1HFjNhhYDEa_xSvay=s64","userId":"11213870514507527976"}},"outputId":"93b2c7e3-5b02-4553-a8c2-66ce2392f804"},"source":["# Gini Impurity of starting node\n","gini_impurity_starting_node = get_gini_impurity(342, 891)\n","gini_impurity_starting_node"],"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"execute_result","data":{"text/plain":["0.47301295786144265"]},"metadata":{"tags":[]},"execution_count":45}]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"gpCQACjgxoaR","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1623566224604,"user_tz":-480,"elapsed":193,"user":{"displayName":"北科大-張嘉芸","photoUrl":"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/AOh14GhcM20C68MTH2x-G3yrqTq1HFjNhhYDEa_xSvay=s64","userId":"11213870514507527976"}},"outputId":"63e55d5a-8d4c-4b21-e695-060e774bc87f"},"source":["# Gini Impurity decrease of node for 'male' observations\n","gini_impurity_men = get_gini_impurity(109, 577)\n","gini_impurity_men"],"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"execute_result","data":{"text/plain":["0.3064437162277843"]},"metadata":{"tags":[]},"execution_count":46}]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"Cp8PhkS2xpn0","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1623566224605,"user_tz":-480,"elapsed":190,"user":{"displayName":"北科大-張嘉芸","photoUrl":"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/AOh14GhcM20C68MTH2x-G3yrqTq1HFjNhhYDEa_xSvay=s64","userId":"11213870514507527976"}},"outputId":"55ddb51d-f83f-4f42-b79f-f2edc68d802d"},"source":["# Gini Impurity decrease if node splited for 'female' observations\n","gini_impurity_women = get_gini_impurity(233, 314)\n","gini_impurity_women"],"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"execute_result","data":{"text/plain":["0.3828350034484158"]},"metadata":{"tags":[]},"execution_count":47}]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"6rdSULyJxq88","executionInfo":{"statu